WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:11.320
Tequila heated to 800 degrees celsius can
be made into diamonds.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:16.720
The snow at the South Pole reflects sound
so well you can hear people talking a mile

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.720
away.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:21.200
Nachos were invented by a man named Nacho.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.420
Human teeth evolved from fish scales.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.860
'Last shake o' the bag' was Victorian slang
for 'youngest child'.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.239
Salamanders can hear with their lungs.

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:39.489
In 1989, a Russian psychic was run over by
a train and killed while attempting to prove

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:42.780
he could stop one using the power of his mind.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.920
Astronaut Harrison Schmitt is allergic to
the Moon.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.600
All the chickens' eggs produced in the world
each year would make an omelette the size

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.590
of Northern Ireland.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.469
When neuroscientist James Fallon studied the
brain scans of murderers using his own scan

00:00:57.469 --> 00:01:01.390
as a control, he discovered he was a psychopath.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.860
There are more than 1,000 species of banana
and we eat only one of them.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.760
John F. Kennedy's brain was removed during
his autopsy and is still missing.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:19.660
For 500 years from the 13th century, 70% of
Englishmen were called Robert, John, Thomas,

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.640
Richard or William.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.880
2.8 million American dogs are on antidepressants.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.250
Traffic lights were introduced 18 years before
the car was invented.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:38.420
80% of people who are struck by lightning
survive.

